.th WHERE I 5/05/76
.sh NAME
where \*- where in the manual can I find this
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd where
pattern
.sh DESCRIPTION
.it Where
searches the tables of contents with the pattern
given, and prints any
lines in which that pattern is found.
This allows a documentation
enquiry without previous knowledge of the exact name, or
section of a command.
The pattern is a
.it grep
pattern, which in turn derives from
.it ed
patterns.
See
.it ed
(I)
for a description of that.
This command is currently implemented as a shell file.
.sh FILES
/sys/man/man/man0/tocx1 through tocx9: the tables of contents
.sh "SEE ALSO"
grep(I)
.sh AUTHOR
Martin Tuori
.sh BUGS
